{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14273014,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":2,"pointsAwarded":2,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57964,"firstName":"William","lastName":"Parker","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO2MGD4gcTFRx970s7DzjQk","sequenceId":15},"course":{"id":76,"name":"Methods of Proof"},"topic":{"id":2798,"name":"Formal and Informal Language"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T20:02:41.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T21:14:43.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T21:15:56.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T21:16:06.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62406548,"created":"2026-10-16T21:14:54.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11935,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":172024,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12752,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>If any two integers are divisible by $3,$ then $3$ divides the sum of the two numbers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the statement above in formal language.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\forall \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z},  (3 \\mid a \\land 3 \\mid b) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid (a+b))$","choice2":"$\\forall \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z},  (3 \\mid (a+b) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid a \\land 3 \\mid b))$","choice3":"$\\exists \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z},  (3 \\mid a \\land 3 \\mid b) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid (a+b))$","choice4":"$\\exists \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z},  (3 \\mid (a+b) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid a \\land 3 \\mid b))$","choice5":"$\\forall \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z},  (3 \\mid ab ) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid (a+b))$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>Let&#39;s examine our statement:</p></p>\n<p><ul></p>\n<p><li><p>The word &quot;any&quot; indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $\\forall.$</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>The sentence refers to two integers. So, by denoting our numbers as $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\\[\n\\forall \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z}.\n\\]</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\\[\n(3 \\mid a \\land 3 \\mid b) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid (a+b))\n\\]</p>\n</li>\n</ul></p>\n<p><p>Therefore, we write the statement as follows:</p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\forall \\, a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z},  (3 \\mid a \\land 3 \\mid b) \\Rightarrow (3 \\mid (a+b))$</p>\n</blockquote>\n","topic":{"id":2798,"name":"Formal and Informal Language"},"example":{"id":12752,"title":"Expressing a Plain English Sentence With Two Quantifiers as a Formal Statement"},"group":{"id":25461,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14273014,"answer":{"id":62406548,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:14:54.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11935},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62406558,"created":"2026-10-16T21:15:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11949,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:15 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":172138,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12751,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>If $x &gt; 3,$ then $x^2 &gt; 9.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the statement above in formal language, given that $x$ is a real number.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\forall \\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\, (x > 3) \\Rightarrow (x^2 > 9)$","choice2":"$\\exists \\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\, (x > 3) \\Rightarrow (x^2 > 9)$","choice3":"$\\forall \\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\, (x > 3) \\Leftrightarrow (x^2 > 9)$","choice4":"$\\exists \\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\, (x > 3) \\land (x^2 > 9)$","choice5":"$\\forall \\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\, (x > 3) \\land (x^2 > 9)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>Let&#39;s denote:</p></p>\n<p><ul></p>\n<p><li><p>$P(x):$ $x &gt; 3$</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>$Q(x):$ $x^2 &gt; 9$</p>\n</li>\n</ul></p>\n<p><p>Then, the given sentence has the following logical structure:</p></p>\n<p><p>\\[\nP(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x)\n\\]</p></p>\n<p><p>This, in turn, is equivalent to </p></p>\n<p><p>\\[\n\\forall \\, x \\in U, \\, P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x)\n\\]</p></p>\n<p><p>where the universal set $U$ is usually apparent from the context. In this case, $x \\in \\mathbb{R}.$</p></p>\n<p><p>Therefore, using formal language, our statement reads </p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For all real $x,$ if $x &gt; 3,$ then $x^2 &gt; 9.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Or, more formally:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\forall \\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\, (x &gt; 3) \\Rightarrow (x^2 &gt; 9)$  </p>\n</blockquote>\n","topic":{"id":2798,"name":"Formal and Informal Language"},"example":{"id":12751,"title":"Identifying Implicit Quantification"},"group":{"id":24156,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14273014,"answer":{"id":62406558,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:15:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11949},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62406568,"created":"2026-10-16T21:15:27.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10059,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:15 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":183558,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12751,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>The square root of $1\\,024$ is a natural number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the statement above in formal language.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\exists \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\sqrt{1\\,024} = n$","choice2":"$\\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\sqrt{1\\,024} = n$ ","choice3":"$\\exists \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, 1\\,024 = \\sqrt{n}$","choice4":"$\\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, 1\\,024 = n^2$ ","choice5":"$\\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, 1\\,024 = \\sqrt{n}$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>Recall that &quot;The square root of $1\\,024$ is a natural number&quot; means the following:</p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There exists a natural number $n$ such that $\\sqrt{1\\,024} = n.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>More formally, this reads as follows:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\exists \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\sqrt{1\\,024} = n$</p>\n</blockquote>\n","topic":{"id":2798,"name":"Formal and Informal Language"},"example":{"id":12751,"title":"Identifying Implicit Quantification"},"group":{"id":25450,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14273014,"answer":{"id":62406568,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:15:27.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10059},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62406611,"created":"2026-10-16T21:15:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9994,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:15 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":183710,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12752,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>For every rational number, there exists another rational number such that their sum is $0.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the statement above in formal language.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\forall \\, a \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\, \\exists \\, b \\in \\mathbb{Q},\\, a+b=0$","choice2":"$\\exists \\, a \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\,  \\forall \\, b \\in \\mathbb{Q},\\, a+b=0$","choice3":"$\\forall \\, a, b \\in \\mathbb{Q},\\, a+b=0$","choice4":"$\\exists \\, a, b \\in \\mathbb{Q},\\, a+b=0$","choice5":"$\\forall \\, a \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\, \\exists \\, b \\in \\mathbb{Q},\\, a+b \\gt 0$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>Let&#39;s examine our statement:</p></p>\n<p><ul></p>\n<p><li><p>The word &quot;every&quot; indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $\\forall.$</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>The words &quot;there exists&quot; indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $\\exists.$</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>The sentence refers to rational numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\\[\n\\forall \\, a \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\, \\exists \\, b \\in \\mathbb{Q}.\n\\]</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\\[\na+b=0\n\\]</p>\n</li>\n</ul></p>\n<p><p>Therefore, we write the statement as follows:</p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\forall \\, a \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\, \\exists \\, b \\in \\mathbb{Q},\\, a+b=0$</p>\n</blockquote>\n","topic":{"id":2798,"name":"Formal and Informal Language"},"example":{"id":12752,"title":"Expressing a Plain English Sentence With Two Quantifiers as a Formal Statement"},"group":{"id":25462,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14273014,"answer":{"id":62406611,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:15:40.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9994},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62406622,"created":"2026-10-16T21:15:55.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11578,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:15 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":183712,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12752,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>There exists an integer number such that any natural number is greater than it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the statement above in formal language.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\, \\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N},\\, k \\lt  n$","choice2":"$\\forall \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\, \\exists \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N},\\, k \\lt  n$","choice3":"$\\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z},\\, k \\lt  n$","choice4":"$\\exists \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\forall \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z},\\, k \\lt  n$","choice5":"$\\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\, \\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N},\\, k \\leq  n$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>Let&#39;s examine our statement:</p></p>\n<p><ul></p>\n<p><li><p>The words &quot;there exists&quot; indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $\\exists.$</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>The word &quot;any&quot; indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $\\forall.$</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>The sentence refers to integers and natural numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $k$ and $n,$ respectively, we have\n\\[\n\\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\, \\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}.\n\\]</p>\n</li></p>\n<p><li><p>Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\\[\nk \\lt n\n\\]</p>\n</li>\n</ul></p>\n<p><p>Therefore, we write the statement as follows:</p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\, \\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N},\\, k \\lt  n$</p>\n</blockquote>\n","topic":{"id":2798,"name":"Formal and Informal Language"},"example":{"id":12752,"title":"Expressing a Plain English Sentence With Two Quantifiers as a Formal Statement"},"group":{"id":25463,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14273014,"answer":{"id":62406622,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:15:55.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11578},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}],"completedStr":"Completed on Fri, Oct 16th","localGraph":{"topicId":2798,"topics":[{"id":2627,"name":"Surjections","prerequisites":[2798],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.8518121577780803,"repetition":1,"stability":0.1502119166530131},{"id":2678,"name":"Injections","prerequisites":[2798],"frontier":0,"halfLife":1.0497324525484129,